nd beer and wine. It operates stores in California, Washington, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Tennessee, Idaho, Maryland, Nevada, North Carolina, New Jersey, Georgia, Ohio, Alabama, Delaware, Kentucky, and Virginia. The company was founded in 1946 and is headquartered in Emeryville, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jason  Potter | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $2.9M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Defensive peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $14K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Grocery Outlet Holding Corp. is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $1.3B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 31%.","The business throws off $24M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -14.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -6.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 70% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7046962808092716},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (31.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 58/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Insiders are net buyers (80% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $3.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive na